* Not unit-testable, needs the on-hardware runbook: everything in
  section 1, pf anchor lifecycle (3.), lease/registry lock race,
  stack up/down, privops symlink canonicalisation.

=== 14. Medium priority — operational quality (features) ===

* (feature) Full base-system update inside a running jail.
  `crate update --pkg-only` (0.8.41; broken today, see 7.) covers
  packages only; the base system is in use by the jail's processes,
  so an in-place freebsd-update is not safe. Needs snapshot → apply
  into a clone (or with the jail stopped) → verify → promote or roll
  back. Interacts with the warm-template cache (0.7.5) and the restart
  policy. Design pass needed first.

=== 15. Out of scope (separate repository) ===

* Admin/dashboard UI for the datacenter view. The hub already exposes
  /api/v1/{nodes,datacenters,aggregate,containers} and the per-node
  crated daemon owns the F2 mutating surface. A richer admin SPA will
  live in its own repository; the minimal vanilla-JS dashboard in
  hub/web/ stays as a built-in fallback (after 8. is fixed it will
  actually show data).

=== 16. Low priority — future enhancements (architectural) ===

* (feature) Layered images — ZFS-based layering through clones
  instead of monolithic .crate archives. Touches create/run/import/
  export simultaneously; the archive format becomes a manifest of
  parent snapshots. Blocked on operator input: canonical layer
  sources, goal (disk vs cold-start vs hub bandwidth), interaction
  with the ZFS-send backup/replicate path and per-user ZFS prefixes.

* (security) True getpeereid(2)-based unix-socket auth for the main
  HTTP API in crated. docs/getpeereid-main-api-refactor.md argues for
  deferring: the per-tenant gate lives on control sockets (Plane 2)
  and the privops socket. The bind→chmod race is closeable with a
  small set_socket-based fix (~50 LOC) — do that as a 1.1.x hygiene
  PR. The big refactor waits for a concrete per-tenant feature on the
  main HTTP API. Operators can scope crated.sock via listen.unix_owner
  / unix_group / unix_mode (0.8.19).

